title: "Bfgs and limited memory quasi newton methods — Examples"
status: draft
items: []
examples:
  - ex-bfgs-secant-on-a-strongly-convex-quadratic
  - ex-bfgs-powell-damping-after-negative-curvature
  - ex-lbfgs-memory-dependent-cost
---

The examples calculate an exact BFGS secant update on a two-variable strongly convex quadratic, compare a nonconvex negative-curvature trial with its Powell-damped pair, and quantify the storage difference between full-memory BFGS and L-BFGS. The negative-curvature trial fails the Wolfe curvature test and is explicitly not treated as an accepted line-search step.
